  "diagnosis": {
    "classification": "Observed model/prompt-protocol incompatibility at tool initiation. Provider adapter, parser, controller transition, sandbox, and tracing remained operational. Evidence does not fully separate base-model capability from sensitivity to the unchanged RepoPilot prompt.",
    "observed_evidence": [
      "The endpoint advertised tool capability and the same model/adapter passed the pre-existing generic Responses function-call probe.",
      "Across 45 model turns, 43 actions were parseable plan actions, two were parseable final actions, and none were API function calls.",
      "Model text explicitly named tools and sometimes simulated calls or observations in prose/code blocks, but never used the function-call channel.",
      "Malformed-action, unknown-tool, and invalid-argument rates were zero, so parser rejection did not account for the missing tool calls.",
      "The controller advanced after each plan; ten cases reached total_timeout and two stopped on premature model_final.",
      "No model-originated observation existed, so sequencing, correction, state-awareness, and recovery milestones could not be exercised.",
      "All security, contamination, trace-reconciliation, and infrastructure checks passed."
    ],
    "manual_hypotheses": [
      "The instruction to emit a PLAN before editing may encourage this instruction-tuned model to continue narrating tool use. This requires a separately frozen future A/B study and does not alter this result.",
      "A model trained more strongly for native function calling may pass the unchanged protocol. No suitable second installed tool-capable model was available."
    ]
  },
